                        <h2 class="blog_heading">1. Let’s start from the basics: What is laser hair removal?</h2>
                        <p>Today, laser hair removal is one of the most commonly done cosmetic procedures. The technician uses high-heat laser beams as a mild form of radiation. Various lasers are now available in India for the effective removal of different hair types for different skin tones and hair types.</p>
                        <p>Laser hair removal uses a light that is absorbed by the targeted pigment in individual hairs. The heat is then transferred from shaft to hair follicle. With heat from laser light, each hair follicle is precisely heated and destroyed and hair can no longer grow from it. Treatment offers a direct delivery method that is more precise in manner. Depending on the area of hair removal, you may need about four to six treatments.</p>
                        
                        <h2 class="blog_heading">2. Why laser hair removal: Is it worth getting laser hair removal?</h2>
                        <p><b>Life-changing benefits of laser hair removal:</b></p>
                        <p>Laser treatment is a speedy process and it only takes minutes to cover small areas like the upper chin. It is also a precise method and can selectively target hairs while leaving the surrounding skin undamaged.</p>
                        <p>When compared to traditional methods (waxing, shaving), the laser process takes care of those painful insightful ingrown hair. Waxing is significantly more painful than removing body hair with a laser. Also for laser treatment, you don’t need to wait and suffer for complete hair growth, required in case of waxing. Rather you will be asked to shave the area before laser treatment, thus leaving you free with smoother skin immediately.</p>
                        <p>When compared with the traditional methods, cost per session in laser treatment is more but it has longer effects meaning lifetime treatment cost is low. Thus, it helps you save money in the long run.</p>
                        <p>Laser and IPL hair removal both work on the same principle. IPL devices are more painful than our lasers and require more time to maintain results. In addition to producing inferior results, IPL devices only work on light to medium skin tones i.e. they severely burn darker skin tones. On the other hand, lasers’ higher intensity makes them better at removing very thick hairs and laser hair removal shows results in fewer sessions.</p>
                        <p>Other methods such as depilatory cream or electrolysis are either quick, short time solutions or require a number of sessions to see the results. Thus laser treatment turns out to be the best solution for permanent hair removal.</p>
                        
                        <img src="../images/laser-hair-removal.jpg" alt="Cost Of Laser Hair Removal in Gurgaon" class="img-fluid">
                        
                        <h3 class="blog_heading">3. Let’s know How Laser Works: How does Laser Hair removal work on our skin?</h3>
                        <p>Let us understand how the laser process works on our hair growth.</p>
                        <p>Hair follows a unique growth cycle and hormonal factor also plays a role in hair growth. Hair follicles are responsible for the growth of hair. They are placed just underneath your skin. When your technician uses a certain type of laser light, pigments in the hair absorb the light and heat travel to the follicles. This heat destroys the hair follicle, and hair can no longer grow from it.</p>
                        <p>If you're considering laser hair removal, it requires some preparation prior to your appointment. You need to shave the desired area, a night before treatment. Do not wax, tweeze or use chemical depilatories between laser treatments. For two weeks prior to your laser hair removal and 2-3 weeks after the treatment avoid any sun exposure. Cause, if you have tanned skin, you may have to reschedule the appointment. Avoid any use of bleaching agents on the skin. Bleaching alters the pigment making it difficult to carry out the laser process. On the day of treatment, keep the skin area free of any cream, lotions, etc. It is also important to discuss your medications with your laser professional. Some medications (antibiotics etc.) can intervene with your laser treatments.</p>
                        <p>Your dermatologist may suggest special numbing gel to apply on the area before treatment. This makes the process more comfortable for you.</p>
                        <p>By carefully following these instructions you will help minimize the side effects and get longer-lasting effects.</p>
                         
