                        <h5 class="blog_heading">10. Side effects and risks of laser hair removal: risks and side effects/complications associated with laser hair removal.</h5>
                        <p>Laser hair removal is a non-invasive technique, generally safe but still may cause a few side effects.</p>
                        <ul class="disc_list">
                            <li><b>Skin patches or rashes:</b> These are usually localized to the area of treatment, such as redness and inflammation of the skin. Most of these are temporary effects and will be resolved in a few days. Your dermatologist may give you certain lotions or creams to minimize the effect.</li>
                            <li><b>Skin color changes:</b> Laser treatment may affect the pigmentation of the skin in the affected area, and the skin may become darker or lighter in color. This risk of laser hair removal can be minimized by using the correct type of laser. A less intensive laser should be used to avoid damaging the skin.</li>
                            <li><b>Severe effects:</b> Although very rare, some people may develop conditions such as excessive hair growth, scarring or changes in skin texture. Eye Injury is another long term and harmful side impact.</li>
                        </ul>
